,{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"accessibilityDropPoint","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"UnitPoint","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI9UnitPointV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"description","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LocalizedStringKey","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI18LocalizedStringKeyV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ModifiedContent","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI15ModifiedContentV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AccessibilityAttachmentModifier","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI31AccessibilityAttachmentModifierV"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[],"type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction_DragView":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction_dragview","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Drags a layer in any direction with momentum and rubber-band bounds. The draggable"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card responds to touch input via Origami’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"origami.Drag"},{"type":"text","text":" patch, which wires its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"output "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"type":"text","text":" to the layer’s transform. When released near the center, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"card snaps back to its resting position."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_DragView","kind":"symbol","title":"Interaction_DragView","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Interaction_DragView"}]},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami","title":"Swami","role":"collection"}}}